## What makes real estate footage look good

There are a few tricks that matter more than people expect.

### Keep motion small
Real estate shots should feel like:
- slider move
- gimbal drift
- slow dolly in

Not:
- drone whip
- orbit shot
- aggressive zoom

### Protect straight lines
Architecture breaks fast when the model gets too creative.

Use:
- gentle depth smoothing
- low video strength
- minimal rotation
- careful hole filling

### Respect foreground/background separation
Parallax only looks good when:
- sofas separate from walls
- tables separate from floors
- lamps separate from windows
- door frames have clean edge depth

If depth edges are bad, fix depth before rendering motion.

### Use multiple short shots
A property video looks better with:
- 4-second kitchen push-in
- 5-second living room pan
- 4-second bedroom drift
- 3-second bathroom detail move

instead of one long shot.

