## Common problems and how to fix them

### 1. Walls bend or “breathe”
Cause:
- too much camera motion
- too much video refinement
- weak depth smoothing

Fix:
- lower `tz_end`
- lower yaw/rotation
- increase depth blur
- reduce video strength

---

### 2. Furniture edges smear
Cause:
- rough depth boundaries
- disocclusion gaps

Fix:
- blur / soften depth map
- expand hole fill
- reduce X/Y motion
- add mask cleanup if available

---

### 3. Windows look broken
Cause:
- bright reflections confuse depth
- background outside the window gets warped

Fix:
- reduce motion
- manually remap window depth if possible
- use conservative hole fill
- avoid strong sideways camera drift

---

### 4. Clip looks fake / “AI-ish”
Cause:
- overcooked motion
- too much hallucination in refinement
- too much prompt influence

Fix:
- rely more on 2.5D render
- lower refine strength
- simplify prompt
- use stronger negative prompt

---

## Best shot recipes for real estate

### Interior hero shot
- slow push-in
- tiny right pan
- no roll
- little or no orbit

### Kitchen
- lateral slide + tiny push
- emphasize island / counters as foreground depth

### Bedroom
- slightly softer move
- shallow parallax
- gentle downward tilt

### Exterior
- sideways drift
- tiny push
- slightly wider FOV

### Bathroom
- very conservative
- avoid strong parallax because mirrors and fixtures break easily

